dev (Turbopack) can hang under back-to-back playwright runs.** Symptom: first navigation succeeds, second test run's `page.goto` times out and `curl` to ANY route hangs indefinitely. Recovery: `pkill -f \"next dev\"` and restart on a different port. Suspect dangling chromium HMR socket from the previous run."," - **react-hooks/set-state-in-effect rule.** A bare `void asyncFn()` inside `useEffect` triggers this even if setState happens after `await` (the linter doesn't follow async boundaries). Gate the call behind a one-shot `useRef(false)` flag (`if (initialRenderRef.current) return; initialRenderRef.current = true; void asyncFn();`) — the linter sees this as a one-time subscription and accepts it. Same gating pattern that GaussDemo uses with its `pendingSigmaRef` ref-check.","-- **Mark a non-Code section \"done\".** PATCH `/api/progress` with `{ courseSlug, lessonSlug, sectionState: { [sectionId]: { done: true } } }`. `applyProgressPatch` shallow-merges into `sectionState[sectionId]`, so sibling fields on other sections are untouched. Section IDs are per-widget-instance, so this is the canonical pattern when there's no `userCode` to persist (Quiz, CodeCloze without user-code, future DragMatch, etc.).","+- **Mark a non-Code section \"done\".** PATCH `/api/progress` with `{ courseSlug, lessonSlug, sectionState: { [sectionId]: { done: true } } }`. `applyProgressPatch` shallow-merges into `sectionState[sectionId]`, so sibling fields on other sections are untouched. Section IDs are per-widget-instance, so this is the canonical pattern when there's no `userCode` to persist (Quiz, CodeCloze, DragMatch, etc.).","+- **Mixing CSS shorthand `border` with separate `borderColor` re-renders trigger a React style warning.** Don't compose `{ border: '1px solid X' }` with a hover override `{ borderColor: 'Y' }`. Use longhand from the start (`borderWidth`, `borderStyle`, `borderColor`) so hover/feedback states only override the longhand piece. Surfaces this in DragMatch zone/bank styles where hover swaps the colour.","+- **dnd-kit (`@dnd-kit/core` + `@dnd-kit/sortable`) is already in `package.json` (added pre-MVP).** `useSensors(useSensor(PointerSensor, { activationConstraint: { distance: 4 } }), useSensor(KeyboardSensor))` is the canonical sensor set for keyboard-accessible drag widgets. `useDraggable` automatically attaches `role=\"button\"`, `tabIndex=0`, `aria-pressed`, `aria-roledescription` — verifying those attributes is enough to prove keyboard sensors are wired without simulating arrow-key navigation in playwright (each ArrowKey only moves 25 px by default and the simulated drag is brittle). For a draggable+droppable bank/zone layout: track `placement: Record<containerId, itemId[]>` with a sentinel `__bank__` id; on `onDragEnd` find the item's source container, splice it out, push into the target. Use `<DragOverlay>` so the drag preview is portal-rendered and unaffected by transforms inside the original layout."," - **Inline syntax-highlight for cloze-style widgets.** Don't pull in CodeMirror with `Decoration.replace` widgets when the only requirement is \"syntax-highlighted Python with inline editable inputs\" — a small regex-based tokenizer (keywords / strings / comments / numbers / fn-call) inside `<pre>` is enough, and React-managed `<input>`s blur naturally without bridging CM state. CodeCloze's `tokenizePython` is the reference implementation. Use CodeMirror only when the user types into the code itself (Code, Sandbox, ParametricExplorer's Python editors)."," - **Status badge selector for browser tests.** `[data-section-id=\"<id>\"] [data-status=\"done\"]` (NOT `data-widget-status`). `StatusBadge` in `src/widgets/Widget.tsx` exposes the value via `data-status`."," - **`type ComponentType` import for `widgetRegistry[type].component`.** When the lesson page's `SectionRenderer` forwards optional widget-specific props (e.g. `progressKey`, `onComplete`) via the registry, narrow the registry's `ComponentType<{ data?: unknown }>` with a local cast: `widgetRegistry.codeCloze.component as ComponentType<{ data?: unknown; progressKey?: typeof progressKey; onComplete?: () => void }>`. Add `type ComponentType` to the existing `from 'react'` import block in `page.tsx`."]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01HvijZxFCLyjDwfofUnujvf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018TwnodDXazjF5Y8Xyz4bFM","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/home/nukeemann/projects/ai_lecturer/.worktrees/US-047/scripts/ralph/progress.txt","old_string":"## 2026-05-03 23:50 - US-046","new_string":"## 2026-05-04 00:15 - US-047\n- Implemented DragMatch widget — drag-and-drop matching for term↔definition / category↔example / label↔diagram. Items live in a top \"bank\" droppable; zones below accept items, optionally multiple per zone with order checked. Submit highlights correct zones (--success-border + --success-subtle) and incorrect zones (--danger-border + --danger-subtle); misplaced items get a dashed danger outline plus an italic \"→ <expected zone label>\" label pointing them home. Explanation rendered below the answer area as a neutral-tone Callout (info) per the Quiz widget pattern. Section auto-marks `done` on first all-correct submission via `PATCH /api/progress`.\n- Files added:\n  - `src/widgets/DragMatch/{schema.ts, sample.ts, DragMatchWidget.tsx, DragMatchEditor.tsx}`\n  - `src/widgets/schemas/drag-match.json` (regenerated)\n  - `courses/dragmatch-test/{course.json, lessons/terms.json}` — smoke-test course\n- Files changed:\n  - `src/widgets/registry.ts` — `dragMatch` entry (Move icon, `--widget-drag-match` accent), `WidgetType` union extended\n  - `src/widgets/schemas/build.ts` — added `drag-match` to widgets map\n  - `src/lib/schemas/lesson.ts` — `DragMatchSectionSchema` variant added to discriminated union\n  - `src/styles/tokens.css` — `--widget-drag-match` CSS var in both light + dark blocks (#8a4a6f / #d094b3)\n  - `src/app/courses/[slug]/lessons/[lessonSlug]/page.tsx` — wired `DragMatchEditor` into `WidgetEditPanel`, added `dragMatch` body branch in `SectionRenderer` with `progressKey`/`onComplete` forwarding\n  - `src/lib/schemas/schemas.test.ts` — discriminated-union case for `dragMatch` + dedicated `DragMatchData` schema tests + `validateDragMatch` correctness tests (single-zone all-correct, single-zone swap, item-in-bank misplaced, multi-zone ordered correct/wrong-order/missing, multi-zone unordered set-equality)\n  - `src/widgets/schemas/lesson.json` — regenerated\n  - `scripts/ralph/progress.txt` — added 3 codebase patterns (done-PATCH list, CSS shorthand vs longhand, dnd-kit sensor wiring)\n- Quality checks: `npm run typecheck` clean, `npm test` 7 files / 136 tests pass (added 12 new tests over US-046), `npm run lint` clean in `src/` (only pre-existing errors remain in `claude/design/source/*.jsx` and `scripts/ralph/skills/playwright-skill/*.js`).\n- Browser test (playwright headless on http://localhost:3025):\n  - Test 1 (`/tmp/playwright-test-us-047.js`): rendered the 3-item / 3-zone DragMatch; mouse-dragged i-var → z-fn (wrong) and i-fn → z-var (wrong) and i-loop → z-loop (right); clicked Submit → explanation Callout visible, `[data-misplaced=\"true\"]` on i-var/i-fn, `[data-misplaced=\"false\"]` on i-loop. Clicked Try again → reset → re-dragged into correct zones → Submit → button morphed to \"Solved\" and `[data-section-id=\"dm1\"] [data-status=\"done\"]` badge appeared. Screenshots at `/tmp/us-047-{1-initial,2-placed-wrong,3-after-wrong-submit,4-correct-placement,5-after-correct-submit,6-status-done}.png`.\n  - Test 2 (`/tmp/playwright-test-us-047-keyboard.js`): focused i-var, pressed Space → `aria-pressed=true` (keyboard lift fired); pressed Space again → drop. Confirms `useSensor(KeyboardSensor)` is wired and `useDraggable` attached `role=button`, `tabIndex=0`, `aria-pressed`, `aria-roledescription=\"Draggable item\"`.\n- **Assumptions made (no human in the loop):**\n  - \"multipleItemsPerZone respected for ordering\" interpreted as: when `multipleItemsPerZone=true`, each zone's `accepts` array is matched with strict order; when `false`, set equality (so author can list multiple alternatives even if only one-at-a-time is allowed). Documented in `validateDragMatch` jsdoc-equivalent and exercised by both test cases.\n  - \"subtle outline pointing back to expected zone\" rendered as a dashed danger-border outline + an inline italic \"→ <expected zone label>\" suffix on the misplaced item. Avoids drawing actual SVG arrows (would clash with dnd-kit's transform overlay) while still naming the destination.\n  - When `multipleItemsPerZone=false` and the user drops a 2nd item on an already-occupied zone, the existing occupant is bounced back to the bank rather than rejecting the drop. Feels less surprising than a no-op for a single-user MVP.\n- **Learnings for future iterations:**\n  - dnd-kit listeners + `aria-pressed` toggle is the cheapest way to E2E-test keyboard accessibility — proving full keyboard navigation requires brittle ArrowKey/coords plumbing because the default `KeyboardCoordinateGetter` only translates by 25 px per press.\n  - `useDraggable`'s `attributes` already include `aria-roledescription`; passing `attributes: { roleDescription: 'Draggable item' }` overrides only the localised string.\n  - Style warning: do NOT mix shorthand `border` (in base style) with `borderColor` (in hover/feedback overrides). React logs a \"Removing borderColor\" warning on every re-render. Switch the base to longhand (`borderWidth`/`borderStyle`/`borderColor`) so hover only touches the longhand it overrides.\n  - For widgets with auto-completion side-effects (PATCH /api/progress + onComplete), gate the call inside the click handler against a `useRef(false)` rather than a `useEffect`. The `react-hooks/set-state-in-effect` lint rule rejects `setState` in effects, but a ref flip + side-effect call inside the handler is both lint-clean and renders the same UX.\n---\n\n## 2026-05-03 23:50 - US-046"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1104,"cache_read_input_tokens":176653,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1104},"output_tokens":69,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"07080243-aa8d-441b-9ce0-ebebd57b013c","uuid":"3713da38-38f7-4406-bb64-a6b84dff09ab"}
