rdering\" interpreted as: when `multipleItemsPerZone=true`, each zone's `accepts` array is matched with strict order; when `false`, set equality (so author can list multiple alternatives even if only one-at-a-time is allowed). Documented in `validateDragMatch` jsdoc-equivalent and exercised by both test cases.\n  - \"subtle outline pointing back to expected zone\" rendered as a dashed danger-border outline + an inline italic \"→ <expected zone label>\" suffix on the misplaced item. Avoids drawing actual SVG arrows (would clash with dnd-kit's transform overlay) while still naming the destination.\n  - When `multipleItemsPerZone=false` and the user drops a 2nd item on an already-occupied zone, the existing occupant is bounced back to the bank rather than rejecting the drop. Feels less surprising than a no-op for a single-user MVP.\n- **Learnings for future iterations:**\n  - dnd-kit listeners + `aria-pressed` toggle is the cheapest way to E2E-test keyboard accessibility — proving full keyboard navigation requires brittle ArrowKey/coords plumbing because the default `KeyboardCoordinateGetter` only translates by 25 px per press.\n  - `useDraggable`'s `attributes` already include `aria-roledescription`; passing `attributes: { roleDescription: 'Draggable item' }` overrides only the localised string.\n  - Style warning: do NOT mix shorthand `border` (in base style) with `borderColor` (in hover/feedback overrides). React logs a \"Removing borderColor\" warning on every re-render. Switch the base to longhand (`borderWidth`/`borderStyle`/`borderColor`) so hover only touches the longhand it overrides.\n  - For widgets with auto-completion side-effects (PATCH /api/progress + onComplete), gate the call inside the click handler against a `useRef(false)` rather than a `useEffect`. The `react-hooks/set-state-in-effect` lint rule rejects `setState` in effects, but a ref flip + side-effect call inside the handler is both lint-clean and renders the same UX.\n---\n\n## 2026-05-03 23:50 - US-046","originalFile":"# Ralph Progress Log\nRotated: Sun May  3 20:56:44 CEST 2026\nPrevious log archived to: archive/progress-2026-05-03-2056.txt\n---\n\n## Codebase Patterns\n- Repo dir is named `US-001` (capitalized) → cannot run `create-next-app .` directly because npm rejects capital letters in package names. Workaround: scaffold into a temp dir (e.g. `/tmp/ai-lecturer-scaffold`), then copy files into the worktree (skip the inner `.git`), and set the package name in `package.json` manually.\n- `shadcn@latest` (v4.x) emits Tailwind v4 / `base-nova` style by default — incompatible with a Tailwind v3 project. Use `shadcn@2.3.0` for v3-compatible init, or write `components.json` by hand.\n- Tailwind v3 baseline = `@tailwind base; @tailwind components; @tailwind utilities;` in `globals.css` + `tailwind.config.ts` with `content: [\"./src/**/*.{ts,tsx,js,jsx,mdx}\"]` + `postcss.config.js` with `tailwindcss` and `autoprefixer` plugins. Theme/token wiring belongs in US-002, not US-001.\n- Design tokens live in `src/styles/tokens.css` (canonical source from `claude/design/source/tokens.css`) and are imported at the top of `src/app/globals.css`. Tailwind utilities resolve through CSS vars, so changing a `--*` value at runtime updates Tailwind classes too.\n- Theme/accent/density are switched by `data-theme` / `data-accent` / `data-density` attributes on `<html>` (defaults: `light` / `default` / `comfortable`). Selectors in tokens.css are scoped to `:root[data-theme=…]` etc. — adding new variants means adding a new `:root[data-…=\"…\"]` block, not a new file.\n- Geist Sans + Mono are loaded via `next/font` (`geist/font/sans`, `geist/font/mono`) in `src/app/layout.tsx`. Their `.variable` classNames define `--font-geist-sans` / `--font-geist-mono`; tokens.css references those via `var(--font-geist-sans)` inside `--font-sans` / `--font-prose` / `--font-display`. Don't hardcode font names anywhere else.\n- Playwright skill at `scripts/ralph/skills/playwright-skill/` ships without `node_modules`; run `npm install --no-audit --no-fund` inside it before first use. Its `detectDevServers()` helper missed our :3000 dev server even when up — fall back to setting `TARGET_URL` manually in the test script if detection fails.\n- **Zod is pinned to v3** (`^3.25.x`) because `zod-to-json-schema` returns an empty object on Zod v4. Don't bump zod to v4 unless the `zod-to-json-schema` import also changes. (Zod v4 has a native `z.toJSONSchema()`, but our AC mandates the third-party lib.)\n- **Vitest needs its own alias config.** `vitest.config.ts` must declare `resolve.alias = { '@': fileURLToPath(new URL('./src', import.meta.url)) }`. Vitest does NOT read `tsconfig.json#paths`. Next + `tsc` + `tsx` (used by `npm run build:schemas`) DO auto-pick it up.\n- **Eslint config does not exempt `_`-prefixed unused vars.** For \"drop one field\" test fixtures, use `const broken: Partial<typeof obj> = { ...obj }; delete broken.field;` — destructuring with `_name` triggers `@typescript-eslint/no-unused-vars` warnings.\n- **Schema layout.** Source-of-truth Zod schemas live in two places: per-widget data shapes at `src/widgets/<Name>/schema.ts`; everything else (Course, Module, Lesson, Section discriminated union, Progress, CourseSpec) at `src/lib/schemas/`. `SectionSchema` is a `z.discriminatedUnion('type', […])` over `'theory'|'quiz'|'code'|'demo'|'sandbox'|'custom'`. Adding a new widget = new folder under `src/widgets/<Name>/` + register a variant in `src/lib/schemas/lesson.ts` + add it to the `widgets` map in `src/widgets/schemas/build.ts`. `npm run build:schemas` regenerates the committed `*.json` files in `src/widgets/schemas/`.\n- **Filesystem helpers** live in `src/lib/server/` (server-only — never import from a `'use client'` module). `paths.ts` exports `coursesRoot()`, `assertSafeSlug()`, `slugify()`, `courseDir/courseFile/courseSpecFile/lessonFile()`. `atomic.ts` exports `atomicWriteJson(path, data)` (writes to `<path>.tmp` then `fs.rename`). `coursesRoot()` honours `COURSES_ROOT_OVERRIDE` env var (used in tests); production reads `path.join(process.cwd(), 'courses')`. Disk layout: `courses/<slug>/{course.json, course-spec.json, lessons/<lessonSlug>.json}`.\n- **Next 16 route handlers + vitest.** Tests can import handlers directly from `src/app/api/.../route.ts` and call them with a synthesised `Request` and `{ params: Promise.resolve({...}) }` (Next 15+ wraps params in a Promise). `NextResponse.json()` returns a real `Response`, so `await res.json()` and `res.status` work in tests. Put the test file OUTSIDE `src/app/` (e.g. `src/lib/server/api.test.ts`) so Next doesn't try to compile it as a route — vitest's `include: 'src/**/*.test.ts'` still picks it up.\n- **Slug rules.** `assertSafeSlug` rejects empty strings and any slug containing `/`, `\\`, or `..` (path-traversal protection). Public slugs are derived from user input via `slugify()` (NFKD-normalise → strip combining marks → lowercase → `[_\\s]+→-` → strip non-`[a-z0-9-]` → collapse `-+` → trim). Slugify can return `''` for all-punctuation inputs; callers must guard (POST `/api/courses` returns 400 in that case).\n- **Pyodide worker singleton.** Web Workers are bundled by Turbopack via `new Worker(new URL('./worker.ts', import.meta.url))` (NO `type: 'module'` → classic worker, can use `importScripts` for CDN bootstrap). The worker file at `src/lib/pyodide/worker.ts` is excluded from main thread imports by virtue of being instantiated only via the URL constructor. Client hook lives at `src/lib/pyodide/client.ts` (`'use client'`) and exposes `usePyodide()`; the worker is a module-scope singleton created lazily on first hook subscription via `useSyncExternalStore`. Subscription on mount = lazy-load contract: dashboards / SSR never trigger worker creation. For id-keyed promise resolution: each `run`/`runWithTests` call generates `req-N`, stores `{resolve, reject}` in a `Map`, and pops on matching `event.data.id`. Custom test runner (no pytest) lives in a Python `__ai_run_tests` function injected once per worker; it `exec()`s each test body in a fresh copy of the user namespace and catches `AssertionError` separately for `assertionDetail`. Test results array shape: `[{name, passed, traceback?, assertionDetail?}]`.\n- **CodeMirror 6 setup.** Packages: `codemirror @codemirror/state @codemirror/view @codemirror/lang-python @codemirror/commands @codemirror/language @codemirror/autocomplete` (commands brings `defaultKeymap`/`history`/`historyKeymap`/`indentWithTab`; language brings `HighlightStyle`/`syntaxHighlighting`/`bracketMatching`/`indentOnInput`). Theme via `EditorView.theme({...})` consuming our `--code-bg/--code-text/--code-keyword/...` CSS vars. Highlight via `HighlightStyle.define([{ tag: t.keyword, color: 'var(--code-keyword)' }, ...])` from `@lezer/highlight` tags. Editor instantiated once in `useEffect(() => {...}, [])` with `EditorState.create({doc, extensions:[…]})`; subsequent doc updates flow via `view.dispatch({changes:{from,to,insert}})`, NOT by re-rendering. Use `EditorView.updateListener.of((u)=>u.docChanged && setCode(u.state.doc.toString()))` to mirror doc into React state.\n- **eslint react-hooks/refs rule is strict.** Never write `someRef.current = value` at component top level — must be inside `useEffect(() => { someRef.current = value; }, [value])` or inside an event handler. Pattern for \"always-fresh closure\" inside a handler set up once: declare `const valueRef = useRef(value); useEffect(() => { valueRef.current = value; }, [value]);` then read `valueRef.current` inside the long-lived closure.\n- **Cmd/Ctrl+Enter in CodeMirror.** Use `keymap.of([{ key: 'Mod-Enter', preventDefault: true, run: () => { ...; return true; } }])` and put it BEFORE the `defaultKeymap` keymap so it wins over Cm-Enter defaults. `Mod` resolves to ⌘ on Mac and Ctrl elsewhere. Have the `run` callback dispatch via a ref (`handleRunRef.current()`) so it always picks up the latest closure.\n- **Progress PATCH for sectionState.** PATCH `/api/progress` with body `{ courseSlug, lessonSlug, sectionState: { [sectionId]: { userCode } } }`. To CLEAR a section's state (e.g. on Reset), send `{ [sectionId]: {} }` — the server's `applyProgressPatch` shallow-merges into existing `sectionState[sectionId]` then replaces it, so `{}` overwrites and effectively wipes the entry's userCode. Caveat: this also wipes any sibling fields (quizSubmission) on the same section, which is fine because section IDs are per-widget-instance. To mark a section \"done\", PATCH `{ userCode, done: true }` together — `done?: boolean` is the per-section completion flag (added in US-011); sending `{ done: true }` alone would wipe userCode.\n- **CodeRunner slots (US-011).** CodeRunner exposes slot props for graded variants without re-implementing the editor/footer: `extraPanel?: ReactNode` (rendered between output panel and footer), `primaryAction?: { label, icon, onClick, disabled, variant: 'primary'|'secondary'|'ghost', testId, ariaLabel }` (replaces ▶ Run; pass `null` to hide it entirely), `onCodeChange?: (code) => void` (mirror doc into parent state), `onReset?: () => void` (parent can also reset its own state when CodeRunner's Reset fires), `outputPlaceholder?: string`. CodeRunner also exports `codeRunnerEditorTheme` and `codeRunnerHighlightStyle` so child components (e.g. inline read-only test bodies) match the editor's look. Read-only CodeMirror needs BOTH `EditorState.readOnly.of(true)` and `EditorView.editable.of(false)`.\n- **TS target ES2017.** The regex `s` (dotAll) flag triggers `TS1501`. Use `[\\s\\S]` in patterns that need to span newlines, never `/.../s`.\n- **Lesson navigation.** Flat ordered lesson list = `course.modules.flatMap(m => m.lessons)`. Prev/next of current lesson is index-1 / index+1 in that list, crossing module boundaries. Client navigation uses `router.push(\\`/courses/\\${slug}/lessons/\\${targetSlug}\\`)` from `next/navigation`'s `useRouter()`. Mark-finished is `PATCH /api/progress { courseSlug, lessonSlug, status: 'finished' }` — applyProgressPatch already handles this and stamps `finishedAt`.\n- **Adding a new widget type = 5 mandatory wiring points** (see `src/widgets/README.md`): (1) `--widget-<name>` CSS var in both light + dark blocks of `src/styles/tokens.css`; (2) Zod data schema at `src/widgets/<Name>/schema.ts` + register in `src/widgets/schemas/build.ts` so `npm run build:schemas` emits `<name>.json`; (3) `widgetRegistry` entry in `src/widgets/registry.ts` (component / label / icon / accentVar) + extend the `WidgetType` union; (4) `<Name>Editor.tsx` per US-023 pattern + import + branch in both `WidgetEditPanel` and `SectionRenderer` in `src/app/courses/[slug]/lessons/[lessonSlug]/page.tsx`; (5) `<Name>SectionSchema` variant in `SectionSchema` discriminated union at `src/lib/schemas/lesson.ts`. Skipping (5) means widget renders but lesson JSON containing it fails API validation. Histogram (US-030) is the canonical reference implementation.\n- **React-aware playwright slider input.** Setting `el.value` directly bypasses React's value tracker — the `onChange` handler sees the *previous* value. Use the native setter override: `Object.getOwnPropertyDescriptor(window.HTMLInputElement.prototype, 'value').set.call(el, '4'); el.dispatchEvent(new Event('input', { bubbles: true }));`. Same pattern works for `<select>`, `<textarea>`.\n- **Pyodide lesson namespace + test isolation (US-031).** Worker holds a Python-side module-level dict `__ai_lesson_globals` (sourced from `src/lib/pyodide/runnerPython.ts` so vitest can re-install it via the `pyodide` npm dev-dep). All `'run'` calls exec'd with `runPythonAsync(code, { globals: lessonGlobalsProxy })` so the namespace persists across Code/Sandbox widgets within a lesson; `'runWithTests'` exec's user code in lessonGlobals (so helpers persist) but each test body in `dict(__ai_lesson_globals)` (so test mutations don't leak). `'resetNamespace'` (new message type, payload `{ lessonSlug }`) calls `__ai_reset_namespace()` which `.clear()`s in place — DON'T reassign the dict, the JS-side proxy points at the original object. Lesson page calls `usePyodide().resetNamespace(lessonSlug)` from a `useEffect([lessonSlug])` so the namespace wipes on every lesson navigation; toolbar `[data-testid=\"reset-session-btn\"]` exposes a manual reset with a `[data-testid=\"session-toast\"]` ack.\n- **Browser tests touching Code/Sandbox widgets must clear `~/.ai-lecturer/progress.json` per-section state first.** Persisted `userCode` (from US-011) auto-loads as `initialCode`, so a stale entry from a prior aborted run silently shapes Submit outcomes. Wipe via `node -e` JSON edit or use a throwaway course slug.\n- **CodeMirror typing in playwright auto-indents on `\\n`.** `keyboard.type('def f():\\\\n    return 42\\\\n')` produces compound indents. Use single-line lambdas where possible; otherwise insert `Enter` + `Home` between lines, or paste via `view.dispatch({changes:{...}})`.\n- **Pyodide batched stdout strips `\\n` (US-032).** `setStdout({ batched })` fires once per line, content only — never join chunks with `''` or consecutive `print()`s collapse into one line. Use the `formatStdoutChunks` helper at `src/lib/pyodide/stdout.ts`: joins with `\\n`, then per-line keeps only the substring after the last `\\r` so terminal-style in-place updates work and bare `\\r`s don't render as extra line breaks under `pre-wrap`. The CodeRunner output panel already uses `whiteSpace: 'pre-wrap'`, so once newlines actually exist in the text, multi-line output renders correctly.\n- **Worker plot capture (US-045 `runWithPlotParam`).** Matplotlib loaded lazily on first request via `loadPackage(['matplotlib'])` then `matplotlib.use('AGG')` (no display server in worker). Cache namespaces by `setupCode` STRING as the key (`__ai_pexp_namespaces[setup_code]`) so identical setupCode runs once per session — the cached dict is copied with `dict(cached)` for each render so user mutations don't leak. Capture the most-recent figure with `plt.figure(plt.get_fignums()[-1]).savefig(buf, format='png', bbox_inches='tight', dpi=110)` then `plt.close('all')` before the next render. JS plain-object payload (`{name: number|string|boolean}`) crosses the JS→Py boundary as a JsProxy → `params.to_py()` yields a Python dict; types are preserved automatically (number→float, bool→bool, string→str).\n- **Next dev (Turbopack) can hang under back-to-back playwright runs.** Symptom: first navigation succeeds, second test run's `page.goto` times out and `curl` to ANY route hangs indefinitely. Recovery: `pkill -f \"next dev\"` and restart on a different port. Suspect dangling chromium HMR socket from the previous run.\n- **react-hooks/set-state-in-effect rule.** A bare `void asyncFn()` inside `useEffect` triggers this even if setState happens after `await` (the linter doesn't follow async boundaries). Gate the call behind a one-shot `useRef(false)` flag (`if (initialRenderRef.current) return; initialRenderRef.current = true; void asyncFn();`) — the linter sees this as a one-time subscription and accepts it. Same gating pattern that GaussDemo uses with its `pendingSigmaRef` ref-check.\n- **Mark a non-Code section \"done\".** PATCH `/api/progress` with `{ courseSlug, lessonSlug, sectionState: { [sectionId]: { done: true } } }`. `applyProgressPatch` shallow-merges into `sectionState[sectionId]`, so sibling fields on other sections are untouched. Section IDs are per-widget-instance, so this is the canonical pattern when there's no `userCode` to persist (Quiz, CodeCloze, DragMatch, etc.).\n- **Mixing CSS shorthand `border` with separate `borderColor` re-renders trigger a React style warning.** Don't compose `{ border: '1px solid X' }` with a hover override `{ borderColor: 'Y' }`. Use longhand from the start (`borderWidth`, `borderStyle`, `borderColor`) so hover/feedback states only override the longhand piece. Surfaces this in DragMatch zone/bank styles where hover swaps the colour.\n- **dnd-kit (`@dnd-kit/core` + `@dnd-kit/sortable`) is already in `package.json` (added pre-MVP).** `useSensors(useSensor(PointerSensor, { activationConstraint: { distance: 4 } }), useSensor(KeyboardSensor))` is the canonical sensor set for keyboard-accessible drag widgets. `useDraggable` automatically attaches `role=\"button\"`, `tabIndex=0`, `aria-pressed`, `aria-roledescription` — verifying those attributes is enough to prove keyboard sensors are wired without simulating arrow-key navigation in playwright (each ArrowKey only moves 25 px by default and the simulated drag is brittle). For a draggable+droppable bank/zone layout: track `placement: Record<containerId, itemId[]>` with a sentinel `__bank__` id; on `onDragEnd` find the item's source container, splice it out, push into the target. Use `<DragOverlay>` so the drag preview is portal-rendered and unaffected by transforms inside the original layout.\n- **Inline syntax-highlight for cloze-style widgets.** Don't pull in CodeMirror with `Decoration.replace` widgets when the only requirement is \"syntax-highlighted Python with inline editable inputs\" — a small regex-based tokenizer (keywords / strings / comments / numbers / fn-call) inside `<pre>` is enough, and React-managed `<input>`s blur naturally without bridging CM state. CodeCloze's `tokenizePython` is the reference implementation. Use CodeMirror only when the user types into the code itself (Code, Sandbox, ParametricExplorer's Python editors).\n- **Status badge selector for browser tests.** `[data-section-id=\"<id>\"] [data-status=\"done\"]` (NOT `data-widget-status`). `StatusBadge` in `src/widgets/Widget.tsx` exposes the value via `data-status`.\n- **`type ComponentType` import for `widgetRegistry[type].component`.** When the lesson page's `SectionRenderer` forwards optional widget-specific props (e.g. `progressKey`, `onComplete`) via the registry, narrow the registry's `ComponentType<{ data?: unknown }>` with a local cast: `widgetRegistry.codeCloze.component as ComponentType<{ data?: unknown; progressKey?: typeof progressKey; onComplete?: () => void }>`. Add `type ComponentType` to the existing `from 'react'` import block in `page.tsx`.\n\n## 2026-05-03 23:50 - US-046\n- Implemented CodeCloze widget — fill-in-the-blank Python exercise with `{{slotId}}` placeholders, per-slot blur validation (exact / regex / oneOf), inline syntax-highlighted code, progressive hints driven by global failed-attempt count, and optional final pyodide-tested code assembly.\n- Files added:\n  - `src/widgets/CodeCloze/{schema.ts, sample.ts, CodeClozeWidget.tsx, CodeClozeEditor.tsx}`\n  - `src/widgets/schemas/code-cloze.json` (regenerated)\n  - `courses/cloze-test/{course.json, lessons/box-blur.json}` — smoke-test course\n- Files changed:\n  - `src/widgets/registry.ts` — `codeCloze` entry (PenLine icon, `--widget-code-cloze` accent), `WidgetType` union extended\n  - `src/widgets/schemas/build.ts` — added `code-cloze` to widget map\n  - `src/lib/schemas/lesson.ts` — `CodeClozeSectionSchema` variant added to discriminated union\n  - `src/styles/tokens.css` — `--widget-code-cloze` CSS var in both `:root` (light) and dark blocks\n  - `src/app/courses/[slug]/lessons/[lessonSlug]/page.tsx` — wired `CodeClozeEditor` into `WidgetEditPanel`, added `codeCloze` body branch in `SectionRenderer`, imported `ComponentType` (used to type the registry-fetched component when forwarding `progressKey`/`onComplete`)\n  - `src/lib/schemas/schemas.test.ts` — added discriminated-union case for `codeCloze` + dedicated `CodeClozeData` and `validateSlotValue` test blocks\n  - `src/widgets/schemas/lesson.json` — regenerated\n- Quality checks: `npm run typecheck` clean (only pre-existing `pyodide` module errors in `src/lib/pyodide/{runner,stdout}.test.ts` — npm dev-dep isn't installed in this env, same on main). `npm test` passes 117 / skips 7 / fails only the same 2 pyodide test files. `npm run lint` introduces no new errors or warnings in `src/`.\n- Browser test (playwright headless on http://localhost:3010):\n  - Filled `aggregator` with wrong \"avg\" → slot turned red, inline `slot.hint` (\"Use the built-in that totals an iterable.\") appeared, and progressive hint #0 (revealAfterAttempts: 1) showed up.\n  - Fixed to \"sum\" → green; filled `divisor` with \"len(values)\" → green.\n  - Submit clicked once Pyodide reached `ready`; finalTests (2) passed in pyodide; submit button morphed to \"Solved\".\n  - Server-side `GET /api/progress` confirmed `sectionState.c1.done === true`.\n  - On reload, the section's `data-status=\"done\"` badge rendered. Screenshots at `/tmp/us-046-{1-initial,2-wrong,3-aggregator-fixed,4-passed}.png`.\n- **Learnings for future iterations:**\n  - Adding a new widget that runs Python via `runWithTests` does NOT need any worker-side wiring — the existing `runWithTests` already exec's user code in `__ai_lesson_globals` (per US-031) and runs each test body in `dict(__ai_lesson_globals)`, so test isolation is automatic. Just call `usePyodide().runWithTests(assembleCode(), tests)`.\n  - For inline syntax-highlighted code WITH editable inputs interleaved, a regex-based Python tokenizer (keywords / strings / comments / numbers / fn-call detection) inside a `<pre>` is much simpler than a CodeMirror `Decoration.replace` widget — the input elements are React-managed and `onBlur` fires naturally without bridging into CodeMirror state. Trade-off: highlighting is less accurate than Lezer, but for the cloze use-case (small templates, ~50-200 chars) it is indistinguishable.\n  - Inline `<input>` width auto-sizing: `width: calc(${ch}ch + 16px)` with `ch = max(value.length, 4)` keeps the input proportional to its content while honouring the 60px min from the AC. Avoid measuring DOM with refs — `ch` units already account for monospace glyph width.\n  - The status badge selector for browser tests is `[data-section-id=\"<id>\"] [data-status=\"done\"]`, NOT `data-widget-status`. The `WidgetStatus` is rendered by `StatusBadge` as `data-status=\"done|progress\"`.\n  - When persisting completion for non-Code widgets (no `userCode` to keep), PATCH `{ courseSlug, lessonSlug, sectionState: { [sectionId]: { done: true } } }` — the server's `applyProgressPatch` shallow-merges, so unrelated sibling fields (e.g. `userCode` from a Code widget on a different section) are unaffected since `sectionId` is per-instance.\n---\n\n## 2026-05-03 22:25 - US-045\n- Implemented ParametricExplorer widget — a generalised version of the Demo widget that injects sliders/select/toggle params as Python globals into a render code block, supports plot/value/both output, and debounces re-renders (default 150ms, configurable via `debounceMs`).\n- Files added:\n  - `src/widgets/ParametricExplorer/{schema.ts, sample.ts, ParametricExplorerWidget.tsx, ParametricExplorerEditor.tsx}`\n  - `src/widgets/schemas/parametric-explorer.json` (regenerated)\n  - `courses/pexp-test/{course.json, lessons/plot-mode.json, lessons/value-mode.json}` — smoke-test course\n- Files changed:\n  - `src/lib/pyodide/worker.ts` — new `runWithPlotParam` message + `__ai_pexp_run` Python helper; lazy matplotlib install with `AGG` backend; per-setupCode namespace cache (`__ai_pexp_namespaces[setup_code]`); captures most-recent figure as PNG and reads optional `result` global as JSON\n  - `src/lib/pyodide/client.ts` — `runWithPlotParam` method + `RunWithPlotParamRequest`/`RunWithPlotParamResult` types added to `usePyodide()`\n  - `src/widgets/registry.ts` — `parametricExplorer` entry (Sliders icon, `--widget-parametric-explorer` accent), WidgetType union extended\n  - `src/widgets/schemas/build.ts` — added `parametric-explorer` to widget map\n  - `src/lib/schemas/lesson.ts` — added `ParametricExplorerSectionSchema` variant to discriminated union\n  - `src/styles/tokens.css` — new `--widget-parametric-explorer` CSS var in light + dark blocks\n  - `src/app/courses/[slug]/lessons/[lessonSlug]/page.tsx` — wired `ParametricExplorerEditor` into `WidgetEditPanel` and the `parametricExplorer` body branch in `SectionRenderer`\n  - `src/lib/schemas/schemas.test.ts` — added schema tests (minimal-valid, select+toggle, debounceMs, unknown-outputType reject) and param-injection serialization tests (slider→number, toggle→bool, select→string, mixed)\n  - `src/widgets/schemas/lesson.json` — regenerated\n- Quality checks: `npm run typecheck` clean, `npm test` 7 files / 116 tests pass, `npm run lint` only pre-existing errors in `claude/design/source/*.jsx` and `scripts/ralph/skills/playwright-skill/*.js` (no new errors in `src/`).\n- Browser test (playwright headless on http://localhost:3008): plot-mode lesson dragged slider 1 → 4.5, plot redrew within debounce (verified by `<img>` src change); value-mode dragged 3 → 5, value text updated 9 → 25. Screenshots at `/tmp/us-045-{plot-initial,plot-after-drag,value-after-drag}.png`.\n- **Learnings for future iterations:**\n  - Pyodide takes a noticeable second (~2-5s) to lazy-install matplotlib on first `runWithPlotParam` — first plot blocks until install + setupCode + renderCode + figure savefig finish. Allow generous timeout in playwright (`waitForSelector('[data-testid=\"pexp-plot\"]', { timeout: 120_000 })`).\n  - The `react-hooks/set-state-in-effect` rule catches `void asyncFn()` even when setState is post-await. Gate with a one-shot `useRef(false)` flag, which the rule treats as a one-time subscription pattern (mirrors GaussDemo's `pendingSigmaRef` gate).\n  - When testing back-to-back lesson pages with Turbopack, the dev server can hang after one playwright run completes — `curl` to any route will then time out. Fix: kill the dev server and restart it on a different port between attempts.\n---\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":42,"oldLines":6,"newStart":42,"newLines":36,"lines":[" - **Status badge selector for browser tests.** `[data-section-id=\"<id>\"] [data-status=\"done\"]` (NOT `data-widget-status`). `StatusBadge` in `src/widgets/Widget.tsx` exposes the value via `data-status`."," - **`type ComponentType` import for `widgetRegistry[type].component`.** When the lesson page's `SectionRenderer` forwards optional widget-specific props (e.g. `progressKey`, `onComplete`) via the registry, narrow the registry's `ComponentType<{ data?: unknown }>` with a local cast: `widgetRegistry.codeCloze.component as ComponentType<{ data?: unknown; progressKey?: typeof progressKey; onComplete?: () => void }>`. Add `type ComponentType` to the existing `from 'react'` import block in `page.tsx`."," ","+## 2026-05-04 00:15 - US-047","+- Implemented DragMatch widget — drag-and-drop matching for term↔definition / category↔example / label↔diagram. Items live in a top \"bank\" droppable; zones below accept items, optionally multiple per zone with order checked. Submit highlights correct zones (--success-border + --success-subtle) and incorrect zones (--danger-border + --danger-subtle); misplaced items get a dashed danger outline plus an italic \"→ <expected zone label>\" label pointing them home. Explanation rendered below the answer area as a neutral-tone Callout (info) per the Quiz widget pattern. Section auto-marks `done` on first all-correct submission via `PATCH /api/progress`.","+- Files added:","+  - `src/widgets/DragMatch/{schema.ts, sample.ts, DragMatchWidget.tsx, DragMatchEditor.tsx}`","+  - `src/widgets/schemas/drag-match.json` (regenerated)","+  - `courses/dragmatch-test/{course.json, lessons/terms.json}` — smoke-test course","+- Files changed:","+  - `src/widgets/registry.ts` — `dragMatch` entry (Move icon, `--widget-drag-match` accent), `WidgetType` union extended","+  - `src/widgets/schemas/build.ts` — added `drag-match` to widgets map","+  - `src/lib/schemas/lesson.ts` — `DragMatchSectionSchema` variant added to discriminated union","+  - `src/styles/tokens.css` — `--widget-drag-match` CSS var in both light + dark blocks (#8a4a6f / #d094b3)","+  - `src/app/courses/[slug]/lessons/[lessonSlug]/page.tsx` — wired `DragMatchEditor` into `WidgetEditPanel`, added `dragMatch` body branch in `SectionRenderer` with `progressKey`/`onComplete` forwarding","+  - `src/lib/schemas/schemas.test.ts` — discriminated-union case for `dragMatch` + dedicated `DragMatchData` schema tests + `validateDragMatch` correctness tests (single-zone all-correct, single-zone swap, item-in-bank misplaced, multi-zone ordered correct/wrong-order/missing, multi-zone unordered set-equality)","+  - `src/widgets/schemas/lesson.json` — regenerated","+  - `scripts/ralph/progress.txt` — added 3 codebase patterns (done-PATCH list, CSS shorthand vs longhand, dnd-kit sensor wiring)","+- Quality checks: `npm run typecheck` clean, `npm test` 7 files / 136 tests pass (added 12 new tests over US-046), `npm run lint` clean in `src/` (only pre-existing errors remain in `claude/design/source/*.jsx` and `scripts/ralph/skills/playwright-skill/*.js`).","+- Browser test (playwright headless on http://localhost:3025):","+  - Test 1 (`/tmp/playwright-test-us-047.js`): rendered the 3-item / 3-zone DragMatch; mouse-dragged i-var → z-fn (wrong) and i-fn → z-var (wrong) and i-loop → z-loop (right); clicked Submit → explanation Callout visible, `[data-misplaced=\"true\"]` on i-var/i-fn, `[data-misplaced=\"false\"]` on i-loop. Clicked Try again → reset → re-dragged into correct zones → Submit → button morphed to \"Solved\" and `[data-section-id=\"dm1\"] [data-status=\"done\"]` badge appeared. Screenshots at `/tmp/us-047-{1-initial,2-placed-wrong,3-after-wrong-submit,4-correct-placement,5-after-correct-submit,6-status-done}.png`.","+  - Test 2 (`/tmp/playwright-test-us-047-keyboard.js`): focused i-var, pressed Space → `aria-pressed=true` (keyboard lift fired); pressed Space again → drop. Confirms `useSensor(KeyboardSensor)` is wired and `useDraggable` attached `role=button`, `tabIndex=0`, `aria-pressed`, `aria-roledescription=\"Draggable item\"`.","+- **Assumptions made (no human in the loop):**","+  - \"multipleItemsPerZone respected for ordering\" interpreted as: when `multipleItemsPerZone=true`, each zone's `accepts` array is matched with strict order; when `false`, set equality (so author can list multiple alternatives even if only one-at-a-time is allowed). Documented in `validateDragMatch` jsdoc-equivalent and exercised by both test cases.","+  - \"subtle outline pointing back to expected zone\" rendered as a dashed danger-border outline + an inline italic \"→ <expected zone label>\" suffix on the misplaced item. Avoids drawing actual SVG arrows (would clash with dnd-kit's transform overlay) while still naming the destination.","+  - When `multipleItemsPerZone=false` and the user drops a 2nd item on an already-occupied zone, the existing occupant is bounced back to the bank rather than rejecting the drop. Feels less surprising than a no-op for a single-user MVP.","+- **Learnings for future iterations:**","+  - dnd-kit listeners + `aria-pressed` toggle is the cheapest way to E2E-test keyboard accessibility — proving full keyboard navigation requires brittle ArrowKey/coords plumbing because the default `KeyboardCoordinateGetter` only translates by 25 px per press.","+  - `useDraggable`'s `attributes` already include `aria-roledescription`; passing `attributes: { roleDescription: 'Draggable item' }` overrides only the localised string.","+  - Style warning: do NOT mix shorthand `border` (in base style) with `borderColor` (in hover/feedback overrides). React logs a \"Removing borderColor\" warning on every re-render. Switch the base to longhand (`borderWidth`/`borderStyle`/`borderColor`) so hover only touches the longhand it overrides.","+  - For widgets with auto-completion side-effects (PATCH /api/progress + onComplete), gate the call inside the click handler against a `useRef(false)` rather than a `useEffect`. The `react-hooks/set-state-in-effect` lint rule rejects `setState` in effects, but a ref flip + side-effect call inside the handler is both lint-clean and renders the same UX.","+---","+"," ## 2026-05-03 23:50 - US-046"," - Implemented CodeCloze widget — fill-in-the-blank Python exercise with `{{slotId}}` placeholders, per-slot blur validation (exact / regex / oneOf), inline syntax-highlighted code, progressive hints driven by global failed-attempt count, and optional final pyodide-tested code assembly."," - Files added:"]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false}}
